>>>Yeah mean in case the BoH gets cursed?
>>
>>It's a cheat (or at least a misuse of the game mechanics). Endgame
>>monsters tend to curse a random item in your carried inventory and
>>having frivolous items in your inventory reduces the odds that one of
>>the critical items (BoH, unicorn horn, your weapon) gets cursed.
>>
> It's not in the slightest a cheat or an abuse. It requires no
> out-of-game knowledge (unlike, say, detailed price id-ing). As your
> character begins to encounter monsters who curse things, or mysterious
> curses that happen after you've killed Rodney, he begins to notice
> that random items from his inventory get cursed, while items within
> containers appear to be safe. He decides to pull some useless items
> out, in hopes that they will be cursed and not something that needs to
> be blessed (such as BoH). What's wrong with that?

While there's nothing wrong with it, the player cannot *deduce* that
it's random and happens the way he thinks it happens (there'd always
be a non-0 probability that the pseudorandom numbers just happened to
satisfy the players hypothesis). A price-IDing table is on the other
hand 100% in-game-deducible.

